#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.api"

Feature: Environment Routing
	Testing the routing of specific tickets to various environments

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1  |
	| Agent1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| 12345678 |
	# Necessary pause after the teardown and the next test execution
	* I wait for "3" seconds

Scenario: Production Environment Routing
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	End users who create requests with any status containing the term production should have their tickets routed to the Production environment.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | T4                         |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    |
	| External ID      | 12345678                   |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_4    | authentication          | production_completely_shutdown                   |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3    | caching_clustering      | production_severely_impacted_inoperable          |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | calendar                | production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions  |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1 | collaboration_suite     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0 | deployment_environments | production_fully_functional_with_observed_errors |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "production"

Scenario: Non Production Environment Routing
	End users who create requests with any status containing the term non-production should have their tickets routed to the Non-Production environment.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | T4                         |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    |
	| External ID      | 12345678                   |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product, component, and system status values
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_4    | authentication          | non-production_completely_shutdown                   |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3    | caching_clustering      | non-production_severely_impacted_inoperable          |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | calendar                | non-production_unstable_with_periodic_interruptions  |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1 | collaboration_suite     | non-production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0 | deployment_environments | non-production_fully_functional_with_observed_errors |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "non-production"

Scenario: Resolution Planning Routing
	Tickets updated with the jira_verified tag should have their sub status updated to Resolution Planning.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | lxc_sm              |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | T4                  |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             |
	| External ID      | 12345678            |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "12345678" with the following tags
	| developer_tools         |
	| enterprise_search       |
	| liferay_commerce        |
	| liferay_dxp             |
	| liferay_portal          |
	| management_tools_lcs    |
	| mobile_device_detection |
	| mobile_experience       |
	| productivity_tools_sync |
	| social_office           |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_developer_tools         |                                        |
	| prd_enterprise_search       | monitoring                             |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_1_1    | apis_integrations_and_extension_points |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_0    | commerce_insights                      |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_1    | configuration_and_settings             |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_3_0    | connectors                             |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_4_0    | digital_merchandise_management         |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_4         | authentication                         |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3         | caching_clustering                     |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_2         | calendar                               |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1         | collaboration                          |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0         | content_management                     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2      | collaboration_suite                    |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1      | deployment_environments                |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0      | document_management                    |
	| prd_liferay_portal_5_2      | liferay_api                            |
	| prd_management_tools_lcs    |                                        |
	| prd_mobile_device_detection |                                        |
	| prd_mobile_experience       |                                        |
	| prd_productivity_tools_sync |                                        |
	| prd_social_office           |                                        |
	And I assign the tickets with the ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" with the following tags
	| jira_verified |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the sub-status "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with the ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should contain the tag "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with the ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should not contain the tag "jira_verified"

